{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenPathFreeze","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"The FREEZE path record: a COMMITTED future-effective freeze, the final __path record of a session. A separate record from IbkrPreOpenPathStatus because its JSON shape was genuinely different, carrying effectiveAtMs and naming its timestamp atMs rather than eventTimeMs and carrying no reasonCodes. Merging the two into one record with nullable fields would have forced AvroJson to emit explicit nulls the browser never saw. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). That topic carried hand-built JSON strings until the 2026-10-18 cutover, which ROLLED IT FORWARD under its own name - the topic was wiped and recreated carrying Avro, not renamed to a versioned sibling: topics in this estate are rolled forward under their own name and versioned topic names are being removed. This record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"state","type":"string","doc":"Always FREEZE for this record. A STRING, not an Avro enum. The strike plane, the path plane and the generation control each draw from a different vocabulary, so one shared enum would have to be the union of all three and would assert less, not more; and a new state would be unreadable to every consumer compiled against the old schema rather than merely unrecognised. The vocabulary is instead closed on the PRODUCER side: each record is built only through its sealed carrier, whose constructor takes the corresponding Java enum, so an unlisted state is unrepresentable at the publication boundary."},{"name":"effectiveAtMs","type":"long","doc":"When the freeze BECOMES effective, in epoch milliseconds. The browser arms its per-strike switching chips only once its server-anchored clock passes this, so it is read by name and must not be renamed."},{"name":"sessionId","type":"string","doc":"Publishing session identity."},{"name":"outputGeneration","type":"long","doc":"The output generation in force when the freeze was committed."},{"name":"atMs","type":"long","doc":"When this record was PUBLISHED, in epoch milliseconds, as distinct from effectiveAtMs. The browser anchors its server clock from the first present of serverTimeMs, eventTimeMs, atMs, effectiveTimeMs, so this field's NAME is part of the contract."}]}